# Runtime Dev Branch Notes — Capability Executor Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-16  
**Branch:** `capability-executor-contract-v1`  
**Status:** Repo-verified on `capability-executor-contract-v1` for the declared contract-only scope after upload; syntax-checked, contract-smoke-tested, helper-checked, artifact-guarded, package-extracted/rechecked, and Michael-run local checks passed. No real-runtime test required for the declared contract-only scope. Main-branch verification remains pending until after merge.

---

## Purpose

This branch adds a contract-only Capability Executor layer under `runtime/execution/`.

The branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
how an approved backend adapter plan becomes a metadata-only execution descriptor;
how the current substrate chain reaches its final pre-execution contract seam;
how action, route, service, and backend metadata are copied into a future invocation descriptor;
how the execution contract rejects executable backend payloads and runtime/worker wiring;
how the execution namespace stays modular rather than collapsing into a single executor file.
```

This is the next substrate step after the action envelope, capability registry, bus skeleton, capability router contract, capability service contract, backend adapter contract, and router namespace cleanup branches:

```text
action envelope -> bus intake -> router plan -> service contract -> backend adapter contract -> execution descriptor
```

---

## Namespace decision

Capability execution contracts live under:

```text
runtime/execution/
```

They were intentionally not added under `runtime/bus/`, `runtime/router/`, or `runtime/backends/`.

Reason:

```text
runtime/bus/ is the controlled action boundary;
runtime/router/ resolves route metadata;
runtime/backends/ validates backend adapter metadata;
runtime/execution/ records the final descriptor seam before future executeAction/backend invocation work.
```

This branch is descriptor-only. It does not execute anything.

