## Modular design shape

The branch follows a deliberately small execution namespace split:

```text
capabilityExecutionCommon.mjs       shared version/copy/prefix/guard helpers
capabilityExecutionPlan.mjs         backend-plan-to-execution-descriptor validation
capabilityExecutorContract.mjs      thin public barrel/export surface
```

The public import surface is the barrel:

```js
import {
    assertCapabilityExecutionPlan,
    normalizeCapabilityExecutionPlan,
    validateCapabilityExecutionPlan
} from "./runtime/execution/capabilityExecutorContract.mjs";
```

The public barrel remains thin. It does not hide implementation logic.

---

## Contract-only guardrails

Execution plans are metadata-only descriptors. They reject:

```text
modelPath/baseModel/mmprojPath/projectorPath fields
backendOptions/adapterArgs/rawBackendPayload fields
toolProcess/command/shell/exec/spawn/cwd/env/stdio fields
function/handler/execute/executeAction/invoke fields
workerBridge/llama_worker/nodeLlamaCpp fields
path-like metadata values for execution metadata IDs
unknown execution-plan and invocation fields
prototype-pollution keys through the shared contract-validation traversal
```

The plan helper returns a descriptor:

```js
const capabilityExecutionPlan = {
    contractVersion: "capability-executor.v1",
    backendPlan,
    invocation: {
        actionId,
        runId,
        capability,
        serviceId,
        adapterId,
        backendKind,
        routeId,
        modelBundleId,
        hardwareProfileId,
        stream,
        timeoutMs,
        resultContract,
        eventContract
    }
};
```

It does not call a service, call a backend, enqueue a request, emit runtime events, stream tokens, or touch native/model execution.

---

## Validation coverage

New smoke test:

```bash
node ./tests/smokeTestCapabilityExecutorContract.mjs
```

Coverage includes:

```text
contract version export;
valid action -> bus action -> route plan -> service plan -> backend adapter plan -> execution plan;
invocation metadata for actionId/runId/capability/serviceId/adapterId/backendKind;
route/modelBundleId/hardwareProfileId metadata propagation;
stream/timeout/result/event contract metadata propagation;
validation of already-normalized execution descriptors;
unsupported execution plan and backend adapter plan contract versions;
unknown execution-plan field rejection;
invalid backend adapter plan rejection;
upstream backend compatibility rejection through the backend adapter contract path;
forbidden model path / backend payload / executable handler key rejection;
copy isolation for nested backend plan and invocation metadata;
source guards for runtime/worker import boundaries;
source guard that the public contract barrel stays thin;
source guard that common helpers do not import plan/contract modules.
```

